;
; Boolean-carry fixture, SPIR-V assembly as the fixture of record: the
; module computes an internal boolean from an early chain intermediate
; (OpFOrdGreaterThan after five recurrence steps), runs the remaining
; over-budget position chain, and consumes the boolean only after the chain
; through a single straight-line OpSelect between structurally unrelated
; arms, so the boolean SSA value stays live across every admissible
; producer cut and the R2VB plan must select BOOL transport in the carry.
; Two properties are load-bearing and assembly-pinned.  The boolean derives
; from a chain intermediate, so an optimizer cannot rematerialize the
; comparison past the cut from a model input.  The select arms share no
; common base-plus-offset shape, so the bcsel survives instead of
; collapsing into float arithmetic -- the collapse that legitimately turns
; the input-derived plus-minus select of the t_bool module into a
; float-only carry in window space.  Reassemble with spirv-as;
; gen_spirv_fixtures.sh validates with spirv-val and embeds the words.
; SPIR-V
; Version: 1.0
; Generator: Khronos Glslang Reference Front End; 11
; Bound: 343
; Schema: 0
